Fuzz targets for the indexedlog on-disk format.

Each target builds one valid structure once per process, then per iteration
writes a fuzzer-corrupted copy of it into a temporary directory and re-opens
it. The input is a sequence of 8-byte patch records applied to the seed files;
see eden/scm/lib/fuzzutil/src/corrupt.rs for the encoding.

  log_open_lookup     Log::open, Log::lookup, Log::lookup_prefix, Log::iter
  rotate_log_lookup   rotate::OpenOptions::open and RotateLogLookupIter, which
                      opens the older rotated logs lazily

Panics, aborts and sanitizer reports are findings. Errors returned for corrupt
data are the expected behavior and are ignored by the harnesses.

Run with buck2. `@fbcode//mode/opt-asan` is what produces sancov
instrumentation; `-c rust.fuzzing=true` on its own builds a blind binary.
Every length and offset in the format is a VLQ, so pass the shared boundary
dictionary:

    buck2 run @fbcode//mode/opt-asan -c rust.fuzzing=true \
        fbcode//eden/scm/lib/indexedlog/fuzz:log_open_lookup -- \
        -dict=fbcode/eden/scm/lib/fuzzutil/vlq.dict -runs=100000 /path/to/corpus

The harnesses call `fuzzutil::configure_indexedlog_for_fuzzing` before
writing the seed, which makes indexedlog use a fixed epoch and skip the
index-lag timestamp, so the snapshot is byte-identical across processes;
without that, offset-based patches into `meta` replayed only by chance.

Steps to run the fuzz tests with the OSS toolchain:

1. Install rustup.
2. `rustup install nightly` to install the nightly toolchain.
3. From `eden/scm`, run `rustup override set nightly && make local` to use the
   nightly toolchain.
4. From `indexedlog` (parent directory of `fuzz`), run
   `cargo fuzz run $TEST_NAME`.

See also https://rust-fuzz.github.io/book/cargo-fuzz.html.
